        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Create exactly one continuous 10-second realistic live-action cable-news split-screen discussion grounded only in the three supplied references. Use exactly two independently tracked people and no one else. <Picture 1> supplies only the locked split-screen news-studio composition, left-right blocking, camera height, backgrounds, and lighting. Do not reproduce its logo, lower-third, branding, captions, or visible text. <Subject 1> is the left speaker from <Picture 2>. <Subject 2> is the right speaker from <Picture 3>. Preserve their faces, hair, suits, shirts, ties, microphones, proportions, and left-right positions.\n\nThe fictional discussion draws on the moral premise of the Injustice comic series: superpowered people become dangerous when their power places them beyond institutional accountability. No superhero, costume, illustration, or B-roll appears.\n\nUse one locked medium split-screen shot with no cuts, zooms, pans, reframing, or transitions. <Subject 1> looks into camera with measured concern and says exactly, “Supermen roaming the country unchecked could impose their will anywhere.” He closes his lips and listens. After a short natural beat, <Subject 2> gives a restrained nod and replies gravely, “If no one can hold them accountable, raw power becomes law.” His lips close. Use natural blinking, restrained head movement, precise lip synchronization, and no overlapping speech. The non-speaking subject remains attentive and silent. End with both men composed and concerned in the unchanged split-screen. Exactly one shot and exactly two English dialogue lines."
      ],
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    }
